---
title: "Pharmacology for Health Information Technology"
code: "HIM-260"
category: "health-information-management"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Emphasizes general pharmacology for Health Information professionals; covers general principles of drug actions/reactions, major drug classes, specific agents within each class, and routine mathematical calculation needed to determine desired dosages. Lecture 3 hours per week.
